  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure will remain anchored over the region through\nFriday. With clear skies and light winds a few locations have\nthe potential for lows in the 30's the next couple of nights.\nThe favored areas for this would be in the Western Catskills and\nNorthern Oneida county. Elsewhere values should end up a bit\nwarmer overnight with ample sunshine warming the entire region \ninto the 60's for daytime highs. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \n\nA Noreaster is still expected to track close to the Eastern\nSeaboard this weekend. Bands of clouds and rain showers should \nmove westward toward the region. Some potential is present for\nthe moisture to make it as far west as I-81. However, our region\nwill also be under the influence of high pressure to the\nnorthwest which will limit how far west the clouds and showers\nmake it. Similar to the previous update, a cluster of ensemble\nmembers does advertise a wetter weekend than what is forecasted.\nFor now, continued with the slight to low chance of showers. \n\nThe Noreaster should exit the region by Monday with high\npressure building in early next week.",
